WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:01.980
Cassiopeia, across the pole.

00:02.688 --> 00:10.924
Go straight on past Polaris, as far again, and you meet a letter W of five stars: Cassiopeia, a queen in the Greek story.

00:11.605 --> 00:19.553
She and the Plough sit on opposite sides of the pole and swing round it like the two ends of a seesaw, so when one is low the other is high.
